==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|lang=enm|trecherie}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lang=fro|tricherie}}, {{term|lang=fro|trecherie}} < {{term|lang=fro|tricher}}, {{term|lang=fro|trichier||to cheat}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|treacher|ies}}

# Deliberate, often [[calculated]], disregard for [[trust]] or [[faith]].
# The act of violating the [[confidence]] of another, usually for personal gain.
# [[treason|Treason]].

====Synonyms====
* [[treacherousness]]

